{"agent":"sz-arch-guards","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":5,"detail":"The baseline inventory assertion builds `expected` from numeric `COUNTERS` files and non-split importlinter files only. It does not account for `tests/guard_baselines/unreferenced_functions.toml`, which is read later in the same test by `_kept_unreferenced()`. With that legitimate baseline file present in the repository, `present - set(PER_MODULE) - split` contains `\"unreferenced_functions.toml\"` while `expected` does not, so the test fails with the “read by no guard” message even though the file is read by a guard.","digest":"93942e7cda52544e","location":"tests/test_architecture_counters.py:test_every_guard_has_its_own_baseline_file_and_nothing_else_is_there","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_architecture_counters.py:test_every_guard_has_its_own_baseline_file_and_nothing_else_is_there"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The split moves collected tests out of `tests/test_architecture_guards.py`. For example, `test_counter_counts_what_it_says` is now defined in `tests/test_architecture_counters.py`, so a previously valid selector such as `pytest 'tests/test_architecture_guards.py::test_counter_counts_what_it_says'` now fails collection with `ERROR: not found`. The manifest contains no documented rename map, so the collected test IDs before and after are not the same set, violating the explicit split requirement.","digest":"11ab88a635868459","location":"tests/test_architecture_guards.py","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_architecture_guards.py"},{"chunk":7,"detail":"This hunk removes `test_import_contracts`, `test_every_extra_has_a_contract`, `test_counter_counts_what_it_says`, and the other moved guard tests from `tests/test_architecture_guards.py`; the manifest re-adds them under `tests/test_architecture_counters.py` and `tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py`. That changes pytest node IDs—for example `tests/test_architecture_guards.py::test_import_contracts` becomes `tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py::test_import_contracts`. The intent requires the collected test IDs before and after to be the same set or a documented rename map. No rename map is present in this part or in the manifest (`docs/ddflow/research/graph-internal.md` changes only one line and is not a test-ID map), so an existing CI invocation or golden pin selecting the old node ID now fails with the test not found.","digest":"c4857a04fdb5eb64","location":"tests/test_architecture_guards.py:537","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_architecture_guards.py:537"}],"chunks_total":9,"coverage":"9/9 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":83567,"diff_sha":"9b817e58350ad9023e028b1556030c63ad34b0ac438c9b536bf5e4d9136d1dda","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":1,"files":1,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1214.5,"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"099e2b13faf546e4","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/SZ-split-test_architecture_guards.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261102T061104Z-aa882d42.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9],"reviewed_head":"eeaedbcd3cc9fbb4daed9052509c70aefbbc035c","reviewed_paths":{".importlinter":"100644 a2fe2c468a15b93fa5f5f8f851478bba27c540a3","docs/ddflow/research/graph-internal.md":"100644 13c8df14b14ede41e40df9a4b10e3a0f73cd3292","tests/architecture_guards_support.py":"100644 8fd126448ce399231ec47c57b3202c31bb69ca6d","tests/file_size_baseline.txt":"100644 5aa2fa8291ae94ae0a68060d79a529d51c1d6d1e","tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-digest-home.toml":"100644 e66f85b824909ea9676f6e8bf69c7f7f3997e875","tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-extras-one-adapter.toml":"100644 a2261edd2b433fcbbde309dba4bb07bc684b16c8","tests/guard_baselines/importlinter-fsio-home/ddflow.infra.fsio.toml":"100644 a7969400076801fbb